## Quick start

```bash
# Start the development stack
make dev-up

# Verify the stack is running
curl http://localhost:3001/healthz
# → {"status":"ok"}

# Check dev environment state
make dev-status
```

## Architecture

<<PROJECT_TITLE>> follows the ASCENT engineering framework (v<<FRAMEWORK_VERSION>>). Key patterns:

- **Containerization-first** — the development environment is the container
- **Make as operator vocabulary** — every operation has a `make` target
- **Backend layering** — `routes → controllers → services → storage`
- **Phase-gated delivery** — numbered phases with explicit go-signals

See [`docs/architecture/decisions/INDEX.md`](docs/architecture/decisions/INDEX.md) for architectural decisions.

## Development

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make dev-up` | Start the dev stack (backend + frontend + nginx + db) |
| `make dev-down` | Stop the dev stack with graceful shutdown |
| `make dev-status` | Full dev environment status check |
| `make dev-logs` | Tail container logs |
| `make test-all` | Run all test suites |
| `make qa` | Run all quality checks (lint + typecheck + structure) |
| `make help` | Show the full SDLC-sectioned operator vocabulary |

